F1 (BLOCK) — packages/cli/src/retro.ts: `classifyAddressedTarget` joins an
unvalidated front-matter id straight onto a path and reads it. Two instances,
one class.

  packages/cli/src/retro.ts:141   const opusPath = join(studioRoot, "opera", `${target}.md`);
  packages/cli/src/retro.ts:154   if (existsSync(join(studioRoot, "decisions", `${target}.md`))) ...

`target` is `addressedTarget()`'s return: the raw capture of
`/^addressed_by:\s*"?([^"\n]+)"?\s*$/m` from a lesson's front matter
(retro.ts:114). `[^"\n]+` admits `../`. Neither site does a containment
check.

The brief states the requirement literally, in the paragraph that specifies
this function (studio/briefs/W-035.md:321):

    "A blank line after the heading and after the list, like every other
     section. Never throws, never reads outside `studioRoot`."

Reproduced (scratch officina, copy of studio/, nothing in the repo touched):

  $ printf -- '---\nstate: "SECRET-LEAKED-FROM-OUTSIDE-THE-OFFICINA"\n---\n' \
      > $S/trav/outside/opera/secret.md
  $ # studio/lessons/L-002.md gains: addressed_by: "../../outside/opera/secret"
  $ bisellium retro --cascade 9 --from in.json --studio $S/trav/studio \
      --now 2026-09-20T09:00:00Z
  $ sed -n '/## Addressed/,/## Proposals/p' \
      $S/trav/studio/acta/2026-09-20-retro-9.md
  ## Addressed

  - "review×mechanical-work-by-hand" → ../../outside/opera/secret (opus, SECRET-LEAKED-FROM-OUTSIDE-THE-OFFICINA)
  - "review×no-builder-isolation" → nothing yet

`draftRetro` read a file outside the officina and wrote its contents, plus
the unredacted traversal string, verbatim into a tracked acta. It also
suppressed that class's petitio (`addressedTarget() !== undefined`), so a
traversal value buys retro silence.

The brief's stated defence ("by the time a retro reads a lesson, `check` has
already blocked an unresolvable value") is procedural, not mechanical:
`runRetro` does not invoke `checkStudio`. Confirmed both halves —

  $ bisellium check $S/trav/studio --level block
    lesson.addressed_by  lessons/L-002.md  addressed_by "../../outside/opera/secret" names no opus, rule id, or decision

check does block it if you run check. The retro above ran to completion and
wrote the file without anyone running check.

This is the officina's own recurrent class `review×path-traversal-from-ids`
(L-004, L-011, L-022) — the class this very opus stamps as addressed by
`path.id.unvalidated` in studio/lessons/L-022.md. P-007's decree is explicit:
"any id or path reaching a filesystem write or front-matter path field goes
through it, a raw join failing review." `path.id.unvalidated` does not cover
this value: `collectIdRefs` (packages/cli/src/rules/paths.ts:49) walks only
`sella`/`collegium` keys plus `probationes` keys, never `addressed_by`.

Scope of the class — searched, and it is confined to these two lines:
  - every `join(studioRoot, ...)` / `join(root, ...)` in retro.ts (13 sites):
    95,164,239,359,404,517 are constant directory names; 213 takes `period`
    from `isoWeek(now)`; 340,430,520,523 are pre-existing (W-018) and out of
