ADVISORY FINDINGS
===============================================================================

A1 (advise) — reds 16 and 17 are not isolated to one behaviour each.
`packages/cli/src/writes.test.ts` and `packages/cli/src/retro.test.ts` have
no `--only` selector (they read only `process.argv[2]` as the repo root),
unlike `rules.test.ts:37` and `rules/lex.test.ts:43`, so both logs record
`# command: node --import tsx packages/cli/src/writes.test.ts .` and both
carry behaviour-16 FAILs. 17 does contain genuine behaviour-17 assertion
failures ("17. answer --opus <unknown>: exits 2 → 0" and a non-identical
petitio), so the builder's account — captured after flag recognition, before
resolution logic — is honest and the red is real. `opus.red_content` does not
fire (the bodies are not identical after header strip). But the engineering
lex's "never two behaviours sharing one output" is only technically met.
Cheapest durable fix is a `--only` selector in writes.test.ts and
retro.test.ts, not a re-capture; it is a separate opus.

A2 (advise) — five officina files are written outside the brief's "Files
owned" list: studio/lessons/L-021.md, studio/lessons/L-022.md,
studio/petitiones/P-003.md, P-005.md, P-007.md. The two lesson stamps are
required by acceptance 3 and 5 and are correct. The three petitio `opus:`
backfills are named verbatim under the brief's Out of scope ("Parsing
`[stated]` prose to backfill `opus:` onto P-003/P-005/P-007. Three files, by
hand, outside this opus."). I checked the values against the `[stated]`
prose and the opera titles and they are substantively right (P-003 → W-020
"lifecycle and evidence writes: bisellium ready, done, red"; P-005 → W-022
"evidence content rules ... (P-005)"; P-007 → W-023 "... P-007 ..."), and
`petitio.opus` accepts all three. Correct work in the wrong opus. Not worth a
revert; worth naming so the next brief's Out of scope is believed.

A3 (advise) — `process.checkpoint HEAD: last commit changed opera without
updating SESSION-HANDOFF.md or dossier progress`. New on the branch, raised
by 1616299 (chore: verify + handoff). A landing-step advisory for the
orchestrator, not a builder defect.

A4 (nit) — docs/ADOPTION.md:126-127 wraps a code span across a newline
