===============================================================================
BRIEF DEFECTS — the spec is wrong, the builders are not
===============================================================================

BD1 — acceptance 3 claims "`lex.unchecked`'s counts drop on all four leges
(today: design 7, engineering 14, production 7, qa 10 — all overcounted
because wrapped markers were invisible)". qa stayed at 10 and Builder A's
flag is correct. studio/leges/qa.md's §2/§3/§4 hold 12 top-level bullets; 3
of them wrap (§2 "One mutation per opus...", §2 "Adopting an advisory-only
rule proposal alone...", §4 "A blocking-rule or lex-wording proposal..."),
and none of the three carries a `(check: ...)` marker on either line. Only 2
clauses in qa.md have a marker at all (`probatio.declared`, `lesson.recurrent`),
both single-line. Folding cannot change a count unless a marker was on a
continuation line, so 12 − 2 = 10 before and after. The brief's "all four"
was an unverified generalisation.

BD2 — acceptance 7 requires docs/ARCHITECTURE.md be regenerated "since
`rules/ids.ts` is a new module edge". scripts/arch-graph.mjs builds a
WORKSPACE graph (`WORKSPACE_DIRS = ["packages","apps","adapters"]`, edges from
each workspace's package.json plus its `@bisellium/*` specifiers).
`rules/ids.ts` is intra-package, so it adds no edge; I re-ran the script and
its output is byte-identical to the block already in the file. The acceptance
criterion's premise is false and nothing was owed.

BD3 — the Timing section pins `packages/commands/src/usage.test.ts` at "30"
scanned usage-constant lines. It is 31 on master (usage.test.ts:73 records
that W-031's `ci.ts` constant moved it). The brief was written against a
pre-W-031 tree. Builder B correctly left the pin alone; the number is
incidental to `ANSWER_USAGE`, which is one line before and after.

